WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.700
- I'm a huge Marvel fan,
I love superhero stuff.

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:04.090
I mean, Eternals is huge.

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:05.760
Being a part of the
Marvel Universe is huge.

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:06.896
Are you so stoked?

00:00:06.896 --> 00:00:08.636
(audience cheers)
- Yes.

00:00:08.636 --> 00:00:09.719
I don't think

00:00:10.918 --> 00:00:11.751
I like,

00:00:11.751 --> 00:00:14.120
I've been getting the
dosages of how big it is

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:17.680
little by little, like
the premier there were,

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:19.670
I just arrive at the red carpet,

00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:23.500
and I started seeing all
these people dressed as us.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:25.140
The movie's not out yet,

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:26.210
and then

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:27.726
Kelly I saw this family, this,

00:00:27.726 --> 00:00:30.770
the father and the mother was dressed,

00:00:30.770 --> 00:00:34.500
they were Latinos as Ajak and
the three little daughters

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:37.570
also like Ajak and they
made their own costumes

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:40.671
and all these girls,
Latino girls were Ajak.

00:00:40.671 --> 00:00:41.754
- I love that!

00:00:41.754 --> 00:00:43.341
- I wanted to cry.

00:00:43.341 --> 00:00:44.286
- That's really cool.

00:00:44.286 --> 00:00:46.310
- I wanted to cry and then I
had to do all the interviews,

00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:48.950
but it really warmed my heart, you know,

00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:49.783
because there is

00:00:50.994 --> 00:00:52.440
somebody that you can identify with.

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:53.550
- [Kelly] Yeah no inclusion like,

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:55.380
and a little kid seeing
someone that looks like them

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:57.420
that can be, they dream bigger.

00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:00.430
That's totally a thing, I
agree, and I think it's awesome.

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:01.530
I think that they are showing more.

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:03.700
This is a diverse cast and
they're showing more diversity.

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:04.980
I think that's important,

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:06.460
especially when it comes to superheroes,

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:08.300
because we hold them so high for children.

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:10.110
You know, like they're always
dressing up as Halloween.

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:11.730
There are all the stories
about them saving the day.

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:14.060
It's like, they need
to look like everyone.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:16.810
(audience claps)

00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:21.980
- Wait a minute, I just saw
myself on TV and it's crooked.

00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:22.813
- [Kelly] You loosening up?

00:01:22.813 --> 00:01:25.030
- Sorry, but the brilliant part is that

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:29.390
being superheroes who were
actually not from earth.

00:01:29.390 --> 00:01:30.840
- Yeah, I know, I love it.

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:34.040
- So it's not about your diversity,

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:37.970
I think it's in this movie it reminds you,

00:01:37.970 --> 00:01:41.440
it's not really even
about where you come from.

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:44.870
It's only celebrating
the difference between us

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:48.960
and what's inside of you
that makes you diverse.

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:52.690
That it's like, what you're made of.

00:01:52.690 --> 00:01:56.480
That is what is important

00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:59.160
for this amazing story.

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:01.520
Not just the geographical point.

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:02.880
- [Kelly] And not just the aesthetics.

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:04.588
- It's not the aesthetics because

00:02:04.588 --> 00:02:08.097
I'm not a Mexican and I'm not from Earth,

00:02:08.097 --> 00:02:11.100
but it's everything about Mexico that

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:14.090
there is a lot to give as a Mexican person

00:02:14.090 --> 00:02:16.590
just in your blood, how you grew up,

00:02:16.590 --> 00:02:21.089
and it's almost like your
energy of what it is,

00:02:21.089 --> 00:02:24.940
your whole history that is valued,

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:27.220
not necessarily the geographical point.

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:28.710
- Yeah, I love that.

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:30.200
I'm so excited.

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:32.110
So wait, what was it like in your costume?

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:34.110
Was it miserable or was it awesome?

00:02:34.110 --> 00:02:36.289
Did you feel superhero?

00:02:36.289 --> 00:02:38.470
- This show is going to give me a bad rep

00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:41.500
because now I'm talking about
all my psychological problems.

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:42.870
I don't know how we landed.

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:44.660
I'm also claustrophobic.

00:02:44.660 --> 00:02:45.772
- Oh my gosh.

00:02:45.772 --> 00:02:48.290
- Stage fright, claustrophobic, and so

00:02:48.290 --> 00:02:50.210
I was terrified of the suit.

00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:51.370
- Oh.

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:53.430
- I was terrified to get in the suit

00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:55.820
and how I was going to be
able to move or not move

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:57.400
and I was I going to get claustrophobic,

00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:59.868
because, you know, sometimes
when I get claustrophobic,

00:02:59.868 --> 00:03:02.020
the first thing is I want
to take the clothes off.

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:04.320
Actually, I actually did it once.

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:07.120
I didn't take it completely,
but I started unzipping myself

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:09.040
in the middle of a movie
because I had to do a scene

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:10.958
on stage with all the people,
and I started getting,

00:03:10.958 --> 00:03:13.010
and I started, and then what is she doing?

00:03:13.010 --> 00:03:13.843
She's taking it off.

00:03:13.843 --> 00:03:14.840
I said, I won't take it all off.

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:16.130
I just need to breathe,

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:19.260
because I was really
tight in that corset dress

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:21.310
and it was just a scene in a movie

00:03:21.310 --> 00:03:22.750
and it just brought it up.

00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:26.720
So I was terrified that I
was going to be the superhero

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:28.690
that went crazy and started stripping

00:03:28.690 --> 00:03:30.120
in the middle of a scene.

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:33.720
I don't take it all off, I
just need room to breathe.

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:35.977
- I just want to thank you
for making me feel normal.

00:03:35.977 --> 00:03:39.459
(laughing)
(audience clapping)

00:03:39.459 --> 00:03:42.537
The fact that you like
are kinda like that,

00:03:42.537 --> 00:03:43.430
and you seem super normal.

00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:45.230
- We're soul mates, you and I.

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:46.063
- I'm like I love it.

00:03:46.063 --> 00:03:48.640
- But it's normal to have
little things here and there,

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:49.950
right guys?
- Yes!

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:52.060
Salma, and awesome,

00:03:52.060 --> 00:03:53.420
weird people are the best anyway.

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:54.253
That's what I say.

00:03:54.253 --> 00:03:55.190
- [Salma] Perfect is not normal.

00:03:55.190 --> 00:03:56.530
- [Kelly] Yes, they're liars.

00:03:56.530 --> 00:03:58.030
- Screw them.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

